{"id":"000VF7","title":"Mind the Edge ! #6","author":"Todd","solvedCount":10,"difficulty":5,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-10-17T17:33:19+00:00","posted":"am 10. Oktober 2026, 11:20 Uhr","rules":"Sudoku: Sudoku with digits 0–8 on each of FIVE 9×9 boards arranged in a plus (center + north/south/west/east). Four corner boards are unused. Within each board, every row, column, and 3×3 box contains each of 0–8 exactly once.\n\nEdge mines: Each digit equals the total number of mines on that cell's four edges (top, bottom, left, right). Each edge holds 0, 1, or 2 mines.\n\nGiven edges: Edges around the given digits are pre-marked:\n\n• blue = 0 mines\n\n• red = 1 mine\n\n• red with a red × = 2 mines\n\nAll other edges are unmarked and must be deduced. Mark remaining edges yourself.(Pen tool under Settings ⚙).\n\nLarge board (desktop recommended): Settings → Experimental → “Test Large Puzzle UI”. Zoom with mouse wheel / trackpad; right-click and drag to pan. Mobile zoom is not supported.\n\nOnline play: https://sudokupad.app/ifkyufx8jq\n\nTIPS: This is a hybrid of Sudoku and Minesweeper. You need both Sudoku rules and the fact that adjacent digits share the mine count on their common edge. For example, an 8 forces 2 mines on each of its four edges, so none of its four neighbors can be 0 or 1. Likewise, none of the four neighbors of a 0 can be 7 or 8.The figure below shows one possible arrangement of digits in a box, together with mines on edges:\n\nMind the Edge ! #0: 000VE7.\n\nMind the Edge ! #1: 000UYM.\n\nMind the Edge ! #2: 000UZC.\n\nMind the Edge ! #3: 000V0U.\n\nMind the Edge ! #4: 000V33.\n\nMind the Edge ! #5: 000VES.\n\nMore of my games: hitodd.com.","solutionCode":"Enter the digits from column 9 of the EAST board (top to bottom).","tags":["Sudoku","Minesweeper"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/ifkyufx8jq?setting-largepuzzle=1","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{"largepuzzle":"1"},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/ifkyufx8jq?setting-largepuzzle=1","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":27,"cols":27,"cages":0,"hasSolution":true,"features":["lines","underlays"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-10-17T17:33:19+00:00"}